CowSwapModule_Fork
├── constructor
│   ├── it should set cowSettlement to the real GPv2Settlement address
│   ├── it should cache the real domain separator from GPv2Settlement
│   └── it should set owner correctly
├── execute
│   ├── given a valid order with real USDC sell token and WETH buy token
│   │   ├── it should transfer USDC from paymentRails to module
│   │   ├── it should approve GPv2Settlement for max uint256
│   │   ├── it should store correct order metadata
│   │   ├── it should emit OrderCreated event
│   │   ├── it should return success with amountOut zero
│   │   └── it should return encoded orderId in data
│   ├── given a valid order with real DAI sell token and USDC buy token
│   │   ├── it should transfer DAI from paymentRails to module
│   │   └── it should store correct order metadata
│   └── given multiple concurrent orders with same sell token
│       ├── it should create independent orders with different orderIds
│       └── it should set max approval to GPv2Settlement only once
├── validate
│   ├── given valid parameters with real USDC and WETH
│   │   └── it should return true
│   ├── given zero sell amount
│   │   └── it should return false with reason
│   ├── given zero target token
│   │   └── it should return false with reason
│   ├── given same sell and buy token
│   │   └── it should return false with reason
│   └── given zero validity duration
│       └── it should return false with reason
├── isValidSignature
│   ├── given a pending order on real settlement
│   │   ├── it should return EIP1271 magic value for valid hash and signature
│   │   └── it should return failure value for mismatched hash
│   ├── given order has expired
│   │   └── it should return failure value
│   ├── given order is cancelled
│   │   └── it should return failure value
│   └── given unknown or malformed inputs
│       ├── it should return failure for unknown orderId
│       ├── it should return failure for wrong signature length
│       └── it should never revert on any input
├── cancelOrder
│   ├── given a pending order with sell tokens in module
│   │   ├── it should return sell tokens to the paymentRails
│   │   ├── it should mark order as cancelled
│   │   └── it should emit OrderCancelled event
│   ├── given multiple concurrent orders and one is cancelled
│   │   ├── it should only return the cancelled order sell amount
│   │   └── it should not affect the other pending order
│   ├── when caller is not owner
│   │   └── it should revert with NotOwner
│   ├── when orderId is unknown
│   │   └── it should revert with UnknownOrder
│   └── when order is already cancelled
│       └── it should revert with OrderAlreadyCancelled
├── estimateOutput
│   └── given valid params with real token addresses
│       ├── it should return minBuyAmount as estimatedOutput
│       └── it should return targetToken as outputToken
├── orderDigestCompatibility
│   ├── it should compute orderId that matches GPv2 EIP-712 digest on real domain separator
│   ├── it should produce different orderIds for different appData
│   ├── it should have non-zero domain separator
│   └── it should match settlement domain separator
├── ownershipTransfer
│   ├── given owner initiates transfer via transferOwnership
│   │   ├── it should set pendingOwner
│   │   ├── it should not change owner until accepted
│   │   └── given new owner accepts via acceptOwnership
│   │       ├── it should update owner to new address
│   │       └── it should allow new owner to cancel orders
│   └── given non-owner calls transferOwnership
│       └── it should revert
├── lifecycle_HappyPath
│   ├── given PaymentRails configures USDC with CowSwapModule and executes
│   │   ├── it should create order and module holds sell tokens
│   │   ├── isValidSignature should return magic value
│   │   ├── given solver pulls sell tokens via settlement approval
│   │   │   ├── module should hold zero sell tokens
│   │   │   └── given filledAmount reports full fill
│   │   │       ├── isValidSignature should return failure
│   │   │       └── cancel should revert with OrderAlreadyFilled
│   │   └── given solver delivers buy tokens directly to paymentRails
│   │       └── paymentRails should hold buy tokens and module should hold zero
│   └── given DAI→USDC order through PaymentRails
│       └── it should complete the same lifecycle correctly
├── lifecycle_CancelPath
│   ├── given order is created through PaymentRails then cancelled
│   │   ├── it should return all sell tokens to PaymentRails
│   │   ├── module should hold zero sell tokens
│   │   └── isValidSignature should return failure
│   └── given order is cancelled then re-executed with new appData
│       ├── it should create a new order successfully
│       ├── new order should have a different orderId
│       └── module should hold exactly the new sell amount
├── lifecycle_ExpiryPath
│   ├── given order expires without being filled
│   │   ├── isValidSignature should return failure after expiry
│   │   └── owner should be able to cancel and recover sell tokens
│   └── given order expires and owner does not cancel
│       └── sell tokens should remain in module until cancel
├── lifecycle_ConcurrentMultiToken
│   ├── given USDC→WETH and DAI→USDC orders created concurrently through PaymentRails
│   │   ├── both orders should be independently pending
│   │   ├── cancelling one should not affect the other
│   │   └── each token balance should be tracked independently
│   └── given three concurrent USDC orders with different appData
│       ├── all three should have unique orderIds
│       └── cancelling middle order should leave others unaffected
├── endToEnd_PaymentRailsIntegration
│   ├── given PaymentRails configures USDC with CowSwapModule
│   │   ├── it should accept CowSwapModule as a valid action module
│   │   ├── it should execute action and create a CowSwap order
│   │   ├── it should return true from executeAction
│   │   └── it should leave module holding the sell tokens
│   └── given order is cancelled after PaymentRails execution
│       ├── it should return sell tokens to the PaymentRails
│       └── it should leave module with zero sell token balance
├── endToEnd_SimulatedSettlement
│   ├── given a solver simulates pulling sell tokens and delivering buy tokens
│   │   ├── it should leave module with zero sell token balance
│   │   ├── it should deliver buy tokens directly to the paymentRails
│   │   └── isValidSignature should return failure after fill is recorded
│   └── given cancel is attempted on a simulated filled order
│       └── it should revert with OrderAlreadyFilled
└── security
    ├── it should read filledAmount from real settlement without reverting
    ├── isValidSignature should never revert on real settlement with any input
    ├── GPv2Settlement should be able to pull tokens via max approval
    ├── cancelOrder should cap return at sellAmount even if module holds more
    ├── duplicate order in same block should return failed result
    └── domain separator should be cached correctly and match settlement
